  "$comment": "GENERATED from the real jscad-raspberrypi V1 TouchDisplay_7inch(rpi) and TouchScreen2(rpi), called with BPlus(2) as the board, reading parts[name].getBounds() inside a checkout of that repository (it is not an npm dependency here, which is why there is no scripts/generate-* companion - see raspberrypi.touchDisplay7inch.spec.js for the exact procedure). Do not hand-edit. All values are millimetres, Z-up. IMPORTANT: these are in V1's BOARD-ATTACHED frame - both factories end by aligning/snapping the whole screen onto the Pi, which this port drops (the attachment is the user's own ui-026 Snap/Align step). That final step is a pure rigid translation, so the spec compares LENS-RELATIVE offsets, which are invariant under it.",
